task: persist-raft-forward (a follower's append forwarded to the leader over the node wire: RaftMsg.Propose / Proposed; NotLeader only when no leader is known)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/persist-raft-forward

why: stage 1a and 1b both name the same limit: propose succeeds only on
  the current leader, a follower answers NotLeader(leaderId) and the
  client retries elsewhere. The node already knows its leader from the
  heartbeats, so the follower can carry the proposal there itself: one
  new message pair on the existing wire (Propose(data, proposer, n) to
  the leader, Proposed(index or refusal) back), the leader appending
  and replicating as for its own proposals, and the proposer's pending
  entry completing when the entry commits on ITS node -- RaftStore's
  pending map is keyed by proposer and sequence already. NotLeader
  stays for a node that knows no leader (an election in progress).
  Laws: the stage-0 suite unchanged (handle gains two cases), the Live
  suite gains an append on a follower applied on every node.
